# River bundle deployment

This rule applies only to handling this extracted River deployment bundle.
Read AGENTS.md and ORGANIZATIONAL-DEPLOYMENT.txt before deployment.
For upgrades preserve the existing S3 connections and IDs, credentials/providers,
config/cache volumes and paths, custom environment, WebP/read/retry settings,
service-account/Secret/TLS references, routing and resource configuration.
Do not replace existing .env/configuration with examples, recreate connections,
import an empty sources array, delete volumes, or modify source imagery.
Enable adaptation by GET/merge/PUT of the existing read-policy settings; change
only mode to adaptive initially, retaining its existing limits and transport.
The included tuning presets are examples for fresh installations, not replacements.
Verify settings and a known existing S3 image after upgrade; keep rollback state.
Keep credential-bearing backups private and out of the shared bundle/results.
Report intentional changes and distinguish cache state and timing boundaries.
